## Why This Is Asked
This tests the ability to design automated containment in a multi-tenant GCP setup with shared VPCs, emphasizing rapid, verifiable rollback and per-tenant boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via IAM Conditions
- Per-tenant VPC Service Controls perimeters
- CMEK rotation and auditability
- Synthetic data for rollback validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy samples (illustrative)
const policy = {
  bindings: [
    {
      role: 'roles/bigquery.dataViewer',
      members: ['user:tenantA@example.com'],
      condition: { title: 'TenantA', expression: "resource.name.startsWith('projects/ORG/datasets/tenant-A/')" }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment under a simulated breach?
- How would changes be audited and rolled back if misconfig detected?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a concrete security control that beginners can implement: tenant-isolated encryption keys and scoped data access, plus safe rotation.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud KMS CMEK, per-tenant key rings
- IAM Conditions to constrain key usage by tenant
- Data scoping in Cloud Storage and BigQuery per tenant
- CI-driven validation and safe key-rotation rollback
- Audit logs and monitoring for misuse

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: decrypt with per-tenant CMEK
const {KeyManagementServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/kms');
const client = new KeyManagementServiceClient();
async function decryptTenantKey(tenantId, ciphertext) {
  const name = `projects/my-project/locations/global/keyRings/tenant-${tenantId}/cryptoKeys/data-key`;
  const [res] = await client.decrypt({ name, ciphertext });
  return res.plaintext;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test a failed key-rotation rollback in CI?
- What are the billing and operational considerations of per-tenant CMEK at scale?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to apply concrete Google Cloud controls for multi-tenant isolation at runtime, beyond theoretical concepts, with a practical path from IAM to data and storage gates.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Conditions for per-tenant API access
- Storage prefixes and signed URLs for per-tenant data
- Per-tenant logging/alerting for exfiltration attempts
- CI gates that detect misconfig and roll back changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple tenant check in API middleware
function authorize(req, res, next) {
  const tenantFromToken = req.user?.tenantId;
  const requestedTenant = req.params.tenantId;
  if (tenantFromToken !== requestedTenant) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CI gate if a misconfig slips through?
- What are trade-offs of per-tenant prefixes vs separate buckets for storage isolation?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, end-to-end thinking for data lifecycle and cross-service cleanup in a real GCP setup.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-based data tagging and discovery across services
- Safe deletion strategies and audit trail
- Backup scrub/retention implications with CMEK
- IAM least privilege and cross-service permissions
- Validation and rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-deletion snippet (conceptual only)
async function purgeTenant(tenantId){
  await revokeTenantAccess(tenantId);
  await purgeCloudSql(tenantId);
  await deleteCloudStoragePrefix(tenantId);
  await deleteFirestoreDocs(tenantId);
  await purgePubSubResources(tenantId);
  await validateNoResidualData(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What if deletion fails on one service after others succeed?
- How would you automate periodic offboarding to ensure compliance and completeness?
